# Where git-identity-check looks for repos: `<path> <depth>` lines. With no lines it looks in
# `~/src 3`, and a file holding only comments counts as missing.
#
# To fill in: remove `#> ` from the suggested line below and change the path to the folder
# holding your repos. The depth is how many folders down the repos sit: 2 finds
# ~/code/<owner>/<repo>.
#
# To check: run `~/.local/bin/git-identity-check --verbose`, which lists each repo it scanned.
#
#> ~/code 2
